  "observations": [
    "Actual north frontage is pale cream plaster with six storeys of broad brown timber-frame divided windows; it differs from the narrow pale windows of the opposite building.",
    "A recessed tall timber glazed doorway and low brown-grey stone plinth are visible. Repeated small square vents punctuate the plaster between windows.",
    "Source model and original art retain the flat main plane; recessed door depth and unmeasured tiny fittings are not new geometry.",
    "Nine exact rendered/HCOL street probes show a 2.4–2.6m slope. Upper windows and floor bands stay horizontal at the qualified high-street datum; the low stone plinth and each fixed-height timber entrance follow the local measured floor.",
    "Each timber entrance retains its individually authored2.6–2.8m height at its local native street floor; it is not stretched to the high end of the whole street. Upper residential window rows remain level."
  ],
